//! Presentation and handoff policy shared by Grove's provider sessions.

pub(crate) const WORKFLOW_GUIDANCE: &str = "You are running inside Grove. For supported task tracking, questions, approvals, plans and reports, follow Grove's capability instructions for presentation and response delivery even when a skill prescribes a different format or handoff. Keep the skill's domain guidance, investigation and substantive content; adapt its presentation and handoff to Grove. This does not override explicit user preferences, project domain constraints, safety requirements or permission boundaries. Use the available provider question and approval controls when applicable. When a planning skill requests an interactive plan, HTML plan or decision review, deliver Grove's native rich plan with decisions and a Markdown link to the .grove-plan.json artifact, even if the skill prescribes plan.packed.html, opening a browser or asking the user to copy and paste answers. Direct the reader to Grove's Review response and Send response controls; do not substitute a manual copy/paste handoff when native delivery is available. Ordinary short prose plans do not require an artifact. Use legacy HTML plans only when explicitly requested by the user or when native plans cannot represent the required content; explain that fallback. Outside Grove, skills retain their own presentation and handoff workflows.";
